   "id": "makkot.23a.8",
   "daf": "23a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "מַלְקִין אוֹתוֹ וְכוּ׳. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? אָמַר רַב כָּהֲנָא: דְּאָמַר קְרָא ״וְהִפִּילוֹ הַשֹּׁפֵט וְהִכָּהוּ לְפָנָיו כְּדֵי רִשְׁעָתוֹ בְּמִסְפָּר״ – רִשְׁעָה אַחַת מִלְּפָנָיו, שְׁתֵּי רִשְׁעָיוֹת מֵאַחֲרָיו.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «One flogs him» with one-third of the lashes from the front of him and two one-third portions from behind him. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters» derived? «Rav Kahana said:» It is derived from a verse, «as the verse states: “And the judge shall cause him to lie down, and strike him before him in accordance with his wickedness, by number”» (Deuteronomy 25:2), indicating that the attendant strikes him in accordance with «one» portion of «wickedness from the front of him,» and «two» portions of «wickedness from behind him.»"
  }
 ],
